      "side": 1,
      "message": "[From Jetski review] On Posix, if a token contains \u0027$\u0027 or other shell metacharacters (such as \u0027\\\u0027, \u0027`\u0027, \u0027;\u0027, \u0027|\u0027, \u0027\u0026\u0027, \u0027*\u0027, \u0027?\u0027, \u0027(\u0027, \u0027)\u0027, \u0027\u003c\u0027, \u0027\u003e\u0027, \u0027[\u0027, \u0027]\u0027, \u0027#\u0027, \u0027~\u0027, \u0027{\u0027, \u0027}\u0027, \u0027!\u0027) without spaces or quotes (e.g., \"-DMSG\u003d$USER\", \"foo\\\\bar\", or \"*.cc\"), escape_quoting will be Some(false) or None. As a result, \"-DMSG\u003d$USER\" becomes \"-DMSG\u003d$$USER\" (which Ninja unescapes to \"$USER\" and /bin/sh still expands as an environment variable), and characters like \u0027\\\u0027, \u0027;\u0027, or \u0027*\u0027 are passed unquoted to the shell. Consider making the quoting check platform-aware (or quoting whenever any character outside the safe set [a-zA-Z0-9_+-./:\u003d@] is present on Posix) so that \u0027$\u0027 and shell metacharacters trigger quoting.",
